    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. but i dont really have any other symptoms like weakness in my arm or leg, or any trouble talking. it just seems like it's just my face. do u think its really necessary to go to the er right now if i feel totally fine otherwise? it seems kinda extreme if it's just a nerve thing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While Bell's palsy can occur without the typical symptoms, the primary concern is still to rule out a stroke or other serious conditions. Your lack of other symptoms doesn't necessarily mean it's not a stroke. If you're feeling fine otherwise, many hospitals and ERs have specific protocols for patients with symptoms like Bell's palsy. To be on the safe side, you can call emergency services to report your symptoms and get their guidance, or go to the ER for a quick assessment.",
